{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011G1afiHjn3mgcJVZ1tyQ6F","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t+++\n2\tid = \"WI-595\"\n3\ttitle = \"LLR-207/TC-205 return and LLR-208/TC-206 amendment: the verdict rows describe every mechanism that now holds them\"\n4\tworkstream = \"process\"\n5\tspecref = \"\"\n6\tbuildtier = \"strong\"\n7\tpriority = 2\n8\tsafety_class = \"spine\"\n9\tbar = \"DevStg-Tests\"\n10\t+++\n11\t\n12\t## Deliverable\n13\t\n14\tFour cells, no new mechanism and no regression written: every arm described\n15\tbelow already existed and passed, and only the record was silent. All four of\n16\tthe spec's claims were re-driven on this tree before anything was edited, and\n17\tall four hold.\n18\t\n19\tRETURNED (`Drafted`, this branch's merge mints their adjudication):\n20\t\n21\t- `LLR-207.detail` — the `governing_rev` clause said the walk peels \"any\n22\t  verified refresh it meets\". `_peel_target` has peeled TWO classes since the\n23\t  second disposable-commit class entered the tree. The clause now names both\n24\t  (the station REFRESH, admitted by `refresh_attestation`; the machinery's own\n25\t  ADJUDICATION CLOSE, admitted by `mechanical_close_attestation` against the\n26\t  exact composed subject, a single parent, and a NON-EMPTY changed-path set\n27\t  wholly under `docs/work/` — the non-emptiness is the code's (`if not paths\n28\t  or …`) and a later read caught the first draft stating a clause the empty\n29\t  set satisfies vacuously, which matters because the zero-path commit is a\n30\t  real class this very test case drives elsewhere), the ONE property that\n31\t  admits them rather than two rules — both\n32\t  machine-authored, both moving the tree without the lane changing what it\n33\t  CLAIMS — and the fail-toward-review direction of every arm. The `work_tip`\n34\t  contrast is now explicit instead of implied: `work_tip` calls\n35\t  `refresh_attestation` DIRECTLY rather than through the shared disposable\n36\t  test, so a mechanical close is never removed by the destructive reset path.\n37\t- `LLR-207.code_symbol` — added `mechanical_close_attestation`, an `__all__`\n38\t  export that changes what both readers answer and that `grep` found described\n39\t  by ZERO rows in any requirements registry. `_peel_target` deliberately left\n40\t  out: private, and the two attestation readers are the named surface.\n41\t- `TC-205.method` / `.evidence` — `THE PEEL` enumerated the refresh arm alone.\n42\t  The second class is now stated in the cell's own idiom, the positive and BOTH\n43\t  refusals, and the three already-passing tests that no test case anywhere\n44\t  cited are cited: the positive (which also asserts the close REALLY moved the\n45\t  tree, and drives the two peels COMPOSING), the hand-written-subject refusal,\n46\t  and the reached-outside-`docs/work/` refusal.\n47\t- `TC-205.tier` — `Smoke` -> `Full`, RULED rather than left open, with the\n48\t  basis recorded in `Method`. 8 of the row's 49 citations live in\n49\t  `test_integrate_admission` / `test_integrate_station`, both in\n50\t  `tests/conftest.py` `SLOW_MODULES` and so deselected by `-m smoke`. `Full` is\n51\t  the cheapest tier at which the whole cited set runs; `Smoke` claimed\n52\t  commit-floor coverage for a set the commit floor only partly runs, which is\n53\t  the direction §12.2 names as the harmful one. Sibling `TC-132` already reads\n54\t  `Full` while citing the same station module.\n55\t\n56\tAMENDED (Approved cells; §A5.2 mints their amendment adjudication at merge —\n57\tno `Status` was flipped and no `docs/archive/last_approved/` was written):\n58\t\n59\t- `LLR-208.detail` — the cell said regen-set membership \"is the only thing that\n60\t  makes the exclusive-writer clause above true\". That stopped being true when\n61\t  the off-trunk refusal shipped, and the snapshot had copied the claim whole.\n62\t  It now states BOTH mechanisms and keeps them distinct, because they hold\n63\t  different halves and neither substitutes for the other:\n64\t  `_off_trunk_refusal` ENFORCES the clause (exit 2 on any branch but the trunk,\n65\t  keyed on the PRIMARY checkout, with `--trunk-step` the one exempt caller\n66\t  because the station's refresh runs the trunk step inside a lane worktree, and\n67\t  `--check` never refused), while regen-set membership keeps the artifact\n68\t  FRESH. The cell records why the refusal is load-bearing and not\n69\t  belt-and-braces: without it the generator returned 0, wrote the directory in\n70\t  a claimed lane, and the work-branch freshness stand-down HID the write.\n71\t- `LLR-208.code_symbol` — added `_off_trunk_refusal` (the row already names the\n72\t  private `_extra`, so this follows its own convention).\n73\t- `TC-206.method` / `.evidence` — stated the refusal arm, including why it had\n74\t  to be driven through a real LINKED worktree (the single-checkout fixtures\n75\t  every other arm uses are their own trunk and keep writing), and cited its\n76\t  detector.\n77\t\n78\tBar `DevStg-Tests` met: full unfiltered suite `1 failed, 3383 passed, 25\n79\tskipped`, the one red being the `docs/stage` FINGERPRINT node, caused by this\n80\tbranch and benign — driven both ways (passes at the integration base, and\n81\tpasses at this tip on a regenerated-stage worktree whose every other derived\n82\tfield is byte-identical, `drafted` included). `docs/stage` is deliberately not\n83\tregenerated on this lane; its freshness is the trunk lane's. Numbers, the\n84\tboth-ways evidence, and the re-run at the closing tip are in\n85\t`docs/log.d/WI-595-llr-207-tc-205-return-and-llr.md`, which also records the\n86\tthree decisions the cells cannot carry themselves: `LLR-208.hat_refs` left\n87\tunset deliberately, the `SR-170`/`UNATTENDED-OPS` question surfaced as a\n88\tseparate finding rather than fixed inline, and the `mechanical_close_attestation`\n89\tempty-path refusal left UNTESTED and named rather than covered, since a new\n90\tregression is outside this return's fence. Nothing was widened into the\n91\tout-of-scope `work_tip` docstring defect the spec fenced off.\n92\t\n93\t## Context\n94\t\n95\tDrafted by WI-590 (its ## Dispositions section) and minted at its merge - drafts-not-mints, ruling R1/R3.\n96\t\n97\tVERDICT THIS CONTINUES:\n98\t`docs/reviews/wi-590-adjudicate-llr-207-llr-208/004-ADJUDICATE-774ef35.md`,\n99\tgoverning line `OUTCOME: RETURN rows=4`. `LLR-208` and `TC-206` were APPROVED by\n100\tthat act; they enter this scope as an AMENDMENT (round 011 MAJOR, below), not\n101\tas a return. NO OVERLAPPING ADJUDICATION REMAINS: `WI-594` (minted at\n102\t`09193fea` for the out-of-band trunk range) was minted naming these four rows\n103\tas well as LLR-209 and TC-207; round 012 drove its first-approval brief and\n104\tfound it would put LLR-207 and TC-205 in front of a fourth adjudicator as\n105\tawaiting first approval, with none of this lane's three returns in the brief.\n106\tWI-594 was therefore NARROWED on the trunk to LLR-209 and TC-207 — the two\n107\trows only that range authored — so this successor is the one next author of\n108\tLLR-207/TC-205 and the one amender of LLR-208/TC-206, and needs no ordering\n109\tagainst it. Its merge mints the amendment adjudication over the two Approved\n110\trows it amends (§A5.2), which is where the approval act is taken.\n111\t\n112\tROUND 011's MAJOR, the amendment half of this scope. `LLR-208.detail` says\n113\tmembership in the trunk regen set \"is the only thing that makes the\n114\texclusive-writer clause above true\"; since `7ea3cce7` that is false in the\n115\ttree — `gen_verdict_rollup._off_trunk_refusal` refuses a direct write on any\n116\tbranch other than the trunk (exit 2), and `trunk_step` passes `--trunk-step`\n117\tas the one allowed off-trunk caller — so the Approved cell now under-describes\n118\tits own module, and the snapshot copied it whole. Amend `LLR-208.detail` to\n119\tstate BOTH mechanisms (the refusal is what enforces the clause; the regen\n120\tmembership is what keeps the artifact fresh), add `_off_trunk_refusal` to\n121\t`LLR-208.code_symbol`, and state the refusal arm in `TC-206.method` with\n122\t`tests/test_verdict_record.py::test_a_work_branch_cannot_write_the_rollup_but_the_trunk_step_can`\n123\tcited in `TC-206.evidence`. Those are amendments to Approved cells: intake\n124\tmints their amendment adjudication at this successor's merge (§A5.2), and\n125\tthe act stays the adjudicator's.\n126\t\n127\t`LLR-207` and `TC-205` return together\n128\tbecause the requirement half and the test half of one gap are the same gap seen\n129\tfrom two sides, and because `staged_drafted_rows` queues an approver only for\n130\trows a delta actually amends — a successor that edited `TC-205` alone would\n131\tleave `LLR-207` with no queued approver.\n132\t\n133\tThis return does NOT inherit WI-586's findings. All of them were re-driven on\n134\tthis tree and all are DISCHARGED: the `governing_identity` HEAD-vs-branch-tip\n135\tclause and the peel-terminus clause now read correctly; every one of `TC-205`'s\n136\t46 citations resolves to an existing, passing test in the file it names; the\n137\t`test_integrate_station` module is cited; the identity-fixture `Method`\n138\tmisstatement is gone; `CMP-006.notes` now names `kitlib/verdict.py (LLR-207)`\n139\tas CMP-008 with `IF-175` as its declared seam; and the `TC-206` trunk-wiring\n140\tgap is closed by a real detector. The finding below is NEW, and it entered the\n141\ttree AFTER the row text was last written: `f4ca1bd5` (\"four batch-lane\n142\tdefects\", merged at `c590637d`) added a second disposable-commit class to the\n143\tgoverning walk; `LLR-207.detail` was last edited at `64692ddf`.\n144\t\n145\tIN SCOPE — two cells, no new mechanism, no regression to write.\n146\t\n147\t1. `LLR-207.detail`, the `governing_rev` clause. It reads \"peeling any verified\n148\t   refresh it meets to reach one those commits would otherwise hide\". The walk\n149\t   does not peel refreshes; it peels through `_peel_target`\n150\t   (`kitlib/verdict.py:431-442`), whose docstring is explicit: \"TWO commits are\n151\t   disposable and this is their one home, so `governing_rev`'s walk asks the\n152\t   question once: the station's REFRESH (which re-merges trunk and regenerates)\n153\t   and the machinery's own ADJUDICATION CLOSE (which archives a judged row\n154\t   terminal).\" The second class is `mechanical_close_attestation` (`:376-428`),\n155\t   admitted by verification against git — exact subject\n156\t   (`station.MECHANICAL_CLOSE_PREFIX/SUFFIX`), exactly one parent, and every\n157\t   changed path under `docs/work/`. Restate the clause to name both classes and\n158\t   the one property that admits them: both are machine-authored and both move\n159\t   the tree without the lane changing what it claims. Keep the existing\n160\t   contrast with `work_tip` intact — `work_tip` calls `refresh_attestation`\n161\t   DIRECTLY (`:466`), not `_peel_target`, so a mechanical close is never peeled\n162\t   on the destructive reset path. That asymmetry is deliberate and is currently\n163\t   invisible in the cell, which is why the cell reads as if one rule served both.\n164\t2. `LLR-207.code_symbol`. Add `mechanical_close_attestation`. It is a public\n165\t   `__all__` export of this module that changes what `governing_rev` and\n166\t   `governing_identity` answer, and grep across every requirements registry\n167\t   returns ZERO rows describing it — so this row is not one of several possible\n168\t   homes, it is the only one. Leave `_peel_target` out: it is private, and the\n169\t   two attestation readers are the named surface.\n170\t3. `TC-205.method` and `TC-205.evidence`. The `THE PEEL` section enumerates the\n171\t   refresh class alone; neither cell contains the string \"mechanical\". Three\n172\t   tests for the second class already exist and pass\n173\t   (`3 passed, 53 deselected`) and are cited by NO test case anywhere in the\n174\t   registry: `tests/test_verdict_record.py::test_the_mechanical_close_does_not_stale_the_round_it_follows`\n175\t   (`:1600`, the positive — a close does not stale the round it follows),\n176\t   `::test_only_the_machinerys_own_close_subject_peels` (`:1628`, the subject\n177\t   refusal) and `::test_a_close_that_reached_outside_docs_work_does_not_peel`\n178\t   (`:1640`, the path-scope refusal). Cite all three and state the arm in\n179\t   `Method` beside the refresh arm, driven as its opposite in the same idiom the\n180\t   rest of the cell uses: the positive and BOTH refusals, so the peel reads as a\n181\t   verified admission rather than a subject match. No new test is needed for\n182\t   this item — the coverage exists and only the record is silent.\n183\t4. `TC-205.tier`, secondary and rulable either way. It declares `Smoke`, but 8\n184\t   of its 46 citations live in `test_integrate_admission` and\n185\t   `test_integrate_station`, both listed in `tests/conftest.py` `SLOW_MODULES`\n186\t   and therefore excluded from `-m smoke` (measured: `-m smoke` collects 56 of\n187\t   139; the 38 `test_verdict_record` citations are the smoke half). The Tier\n188\t   field and the pytest marker are a KNOWN unreconciled pair\n189\t   (`docs/registry-machinery-reference.md` §12.2) that no check compares, and\n190\t   sibling `TC-132` cites the same station module at `Tier = \"Full\"`. Either\n191\t   re-tier this row to `Full` or record in `Method` why `Smoke` is the honest\n192\t   label for a citation set the cheap gate only partly runs. Do not silently\n193\t   leave both readings available.\n194\t\n195\tNOT IN SCOPE, recorded so a successor does not widen: the module's own\n196\tdocstring contract paragraph and `work_tip`'s docstring (`:448-455`) also\n197\tpredate `f4ca1bd5` — `work_tip`'s still claims \"`governing_identity` measures\n198\tcode-time here\", which is false since `governing_identity` calls\n199\t`governing_rev`. That is a source-comment defect, not a spine cell, and it\n200\tbelongs to a code lane rather than to this spine return.\n201\t\n202\tNOT ON THIS LANE: this disposition is a DRAFT. Intake mints it at this row's\n203\tmerge; the lane does not file it.\n204\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff75a583-5561-4a37-8d27-bf441104f2c0","uuid":"19e84b8f-1dfb-4d41-8ed4-b45132b91dce","timestamp":"2026-09-05T00:54:58.248Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template-drive/wi-595-llr-207-tc-205-return-and-llr/docs/archive/work/complete/WI-595-llr-207-tc-205-return-and-llr.md","content":"+++\nid = \"WI-595\"\ntitle = \"LLR-207/TC-205 return and LLR-208/TC-206 amendment: the verdict rows describe every mechanism that now holds them\"\nworkstream = \"process\"\nspecref = \"\"\nbuildtier = \"strong\"\npriority = 2\nsafety_class = \"spine\"\nbar = \"DevStg-Tests\"\n+++\n\n## Deliverable\n\nFour cells, no new mechanism and no regression written: every arm described\nbelow already existed and passed, and only the record was silent. All four of\nthe spec's claims were re-driven on this tree before anything was edited, and\nall four hold.\n\nRETURNED (`Drafted`, this branch's merge mints their adjudication):\n\n- `LLR-207.detail` — the `governing_rev` clause said the walk peels \"any\n  verified refresh it meets\". `_peel_target` has peeled TWO classes since the\n  second disposable-commit class entered the tree. The clause now names both\n  (the station REFRESH, admitted by `refresh_attestation`; the machinery's own\n  ADJUDICATION CLOSE, admitted by `mechanical_close_attestation` against the\n  exact composed subject, a single parent, and a NON-EMPTY changed-path set\n  wholly under `docs/work/` — the non-emptiness is the code's (`if not paths\n  or …`) and a later read caught the first draft stating a clause the empty\n  set satisfies vacuously, which matters because the zero-path commit is a\n  real class this very test case drives elsewhere), the ONE pro