5.method` states the third refusal and why the gate assertion is deliberately absent; and `LLR-207.detail`'s \"can only ask for more\" — overstated in this same spot — is now \"can never ask for LESS\" with the empty arm's equality named.\n\nTwo things worth flagging:\n\n- **The `format` check skips on every commit here** — the pre-commit hook uses `/usr/local/bin/python3`, which has no ruff, and the hook prints its own \"a bar that is not being run\" banner. I ran ruff manually via the primary repo's venv (`format`/`check` both clean), but this lane is structurally not being graded by that step.\n- No `Status` was flipped and no `docs/archive/last_approved/` written — `LLR-207`/`TC-205` remain `Drafted`, and the approval brief is regenerated so what I authored reaches the surface that approves it.\n\nThe final commit carrying the `WI: WI-595` trailer is still owed — I'm holding it until the full suite confirms green, so the trailer isn't claiming a result I haven't produced."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":402,"cache_read_input_tokens":111271,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":402},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff75a583-5561-4a37-8d27-bf441104f2c0","uuid":"acd48560-8b07-46e2-bba3-16b5bc014e54","request_id":"req_011CejPp88odz5RuBqiqgzuT"}
